at was built. Branch epics are not main-plan nodes, so docs depends on the main-plan implementations, which (with E001) gate all branch work transitively |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008, E001 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 3 | Topology outcome selects which branch exists (`remove` if the other outcome holds) |\n| E002 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 6 | Productization code lands in the midstream repo |\n| E003 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 9 | Productized images carry license-cleared dependencies |\n| BRANCH-A-E008 → BRANCH-A-E009, BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 13 | Platform Operator enablement builds against the CRs/manifests the productization epic produces |\n| (no edge) E004 ↔ BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding and general implementation run in parallel; coupling enforced by \"build pipeline green\" AC |\n| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002, E001 ∥ E003 | Rules 14/17 | Topology investigation, repo fork, and license scan have independent inputs; the repo and license work is topology-independent |\n| (no edge) E005 ∥ E006 ∥ E004 | Rules 14/15 | Different repos/areas, no shared artifacts |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Covered by |\n|---|---|---|\n| HLR-1 — supported Feature Store enablement via Platform Operator with productized images | P0 | E002, E003, E004 (onboarding + productized image chain); BRANCH-A-E008 + BRANCH-A-E009 or BRANCH-B-E008 + BRANCH-B-E009 (topology-specific deployment and enablement, exactly one branch executes) |\n| HLR-2 — Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | P1 | E005 |\n| HLR-3 — Dashboard shows Feature Store, links to endpoints per project | P1 | E006 |\n| HLR-4 — product documentation (enablement, getting started, limits) | P2 | E007 |\n\nAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E001–E004 inherit P0\nfrom HLR-1 (E001 blocks all P0 work → implicitly P0). E007 is a `docs-authoring` epic:\npriority-exception applies — strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (not\ninherited from the implementations it depends