w component | No → full onboarding chain (Rule 20) |\n41\t| Platform Operator | Enable Feature Store like other managed components | RHOAI Platform Operator (inferred) | Active | No context file, but the strategy explicitly frames it as the existing enablement mechanism (\"like any other managed component\") — treated as existing, no onboarding chain (see Health Warnings) |\n42\t| Notebooks | Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image | RHOAI Notebooks (inferred) | Active | No context file; strategy refers to existing \"supported workbench image\" — treated as existing |\n43\t| Dashboard | Show Feature Store as enabled component, per-project endpoint links | RHOAI Dashboard (per architecture context) | Active | Yes (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`) |\n44\t| Documentation | New doc topics: enablement, getting started, supported limits | RHOAI Documentation (inferred) | Active — substantive content authoring → separate `docs-authoring` epic | No context file; handled as docs-authoring, not an onboarding chain |\n45\t\n46\tComponent name mapping: all components matched canonical names in\n47\t`.context/rhai-components.txt` exactly; no non-obvious mappings.\n48\t\n49\t## Step 3 — Unknowns\n50\t\n51\tSystematic scan (open questions table, risks, assumptions, pending reviews, conditional\n52\tADRs) found exactly one unknown:\n53\t\n54\t1. **Feast deployment topology** (Open Questions #1): operator-based deployment vs\n55\t   standalone server per project. The answer changes which downstream epics exist and\n56\t   what they do (Feature Store packaging, Platform Operator enablement mechanics, and\n57\t   the Dashboard's data source for enabled state and per-project endpoints) →\n58\t   **Investigation epic E001**, gating the downstream work. Two bounded outcomes →\n59\t   conditional decomposition branches (A: operator-based, B: standalone server per\n60\t   project).\n61\t\n62\tNo other open questions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs exist in the strategy.\n63\tVersion pinning of the Feast SDK against the productized server is an implementation\n64\tdetail (AC on the workbench-image epic), not a genuine unknown.\n65\t\n66\t## Epic List (main plan)\n67\t\n68\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n69\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Select the Feast deployment topology for productization | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Onboard the Feast midstream repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n72\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | Validate licenses for Feast and the Feast SDK dependency tree | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Onboard the Feast repository to the Konflux build pipeline | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Preinstall the Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Surface the Feature Store in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E007 | Document Feature Store enablement, getting started, and supported limits | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n77\t\n78\t### Conditional branch epics (not standalone Jira issues; attached to E001 as plan)\n79\t\n80\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Gate |\n81\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n82\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E008 | Productize the Feast operator-based deployment | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 | E001 outcome = operator-based |\n83\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 | Enable the Feature Store through the Platform Operator (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | E001 outcome = operator-based |\n84\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E008 | Productize the Feast standalone server per project | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 | E001 outcome = standalone server |\n85\t|