 fallback_approach: If the operator-based topology is not selected, this epic is\n    removed; the standalone-server-per-project branch covers the equivalent productization\n    work.\nai_signals:\n  change_specificity: 0\n  pattern_precedent: 1\n  adapter_pattern: 1\n  existing_foundation: 1\n  open_questions: 1\n  external_dependency: 0\n  human_process_gates: 0\n  repo_access: 1\n  architecture_claims: 0\nimplementation_type: null\ninvestigation_signals: null\nai_implementability: High\nai_implementability_score: 5\njira_key: null\n---\n# Productize the Feast operator-based deployment\n\n## Description\n\nPackage Feast for the operator-based deployment topology (if that is the topology\nselected by the Feast deployment-topology investigation): productized container\nimages and deployment manifests for the Feast operator and its operands, so the\nFeature Store can be installed as a managed platform component.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Productized container images for the Feast operator and its operands, built from\n  the midstream Feast repository through the Konflux build pipeline.\n- Deployment manifests and RBAC for installing the operator on the platform.\n- Validation of multi-project behavior of the operator-managed deployment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Productized images for the Feast operator and operands build green through the\n  Konflux pipeline.\n- Deployment manifests install the Feast operator on a test cluster.\n- Operator manages Feast resources across projects as designed.\n- Images carry only license-cleared dependencies.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1: supported Feature Store with productized images, operator-based topology.\n\n===== RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009-ai-signals.md =====\n# AI Signal Rationale — RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 (Implementation, branch A)\n\n| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| change_specificity | 1 | Enablement follows the Platform Operator's established managed-component switch pattern, mirroring how other co