{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99efab5802954402","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9006\n3\ttitle: Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tCustomers building recommendation and fraud models ask for a supported feature\n14\tstore; today they self-manage upstream Feast next to the platform with no\n15\tlifecycle integration, no supported images, and no UI presence. Feast has a\n16\tJira component reserved (Feature Store) but is not yet part of the platform:\n17\tthere is no productized repository, no build pipeline, and no operator\n18\tintegration. This strategy brings Feast in as a supported, installable RHOAI\n19\tcomponent.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast) through the Platform Operator like any other managed component, with productized images. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Data scientists can reach the feature store from workbenches with the Feast SDK preinstalled in at least one supported workbench image. |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P1 | The Dashboard shows the Feature Store as an enabled component and links users to its endpoints per project. |\n28\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Product documentation covers enablement, a getting-started walkthrough, and supported limits. |\n29\t\n30\t## Affected Components\n31\t\n32\t- Feature Store\n33\t- Dashboard\n34\t- Platform Operator\n35\t- Documentation\n36\t\n37\t## Out of Scope\n38\t\n39\t- A feature-authoring UI in the Dashboard (link-out only this release)\n40\t- Managed offline-store infrastructure — customers bring their own storage\n41\t\n42\t## Open Questions\n43\t\n44\t1. Which Feast deployment topology do we productize first — the operator-based\n45\t   deployment or the standalone server per project? Upstream supports both;\n46\t   supportability differs.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bab1b4b1fd3bb0e","agent_id":"a1dd247983ed9ba4c","session_id":"b8ab611b-1533-4a10-b1ed-c369c3109b5b","uuid":"7197113a-69a9-47d5-8dcf-7e17deaa1ffa","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:40:34.751Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99efab5802954402","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
