he build pipeline is gated by the\n139\t\"build pipeline green\" AC on the productization epic, not by a DAG edge. Branch\n140\tepics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n141\t\n142\t## DAG Justification\n143\t\n144\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n145\t|---|---|---|\n146\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | Konflux pipeline needs the midstream repo to exist |\n147\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | Feast SDK and its transitive deps must be license-cleared before shipping in a supported workbench image |\n148\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Dashboard's data source for enabled state and per-project endpoints depends on the topology outcome (true gate, `rewrite`) |\n149\t| E002 → E007, E003 → E007, E004 → E007, E005 → E007, E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all main-plan Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Branch epics are not main-plan nodes, so docs cannot depend on them directly; of the main-plan epics, only E001, E002, and E003 gate branch work transitively — the docs' validation against a deployed Feature Store (output of the selected branch) is sequenced by the gate design rather than by a DAG edge, the only rule-compliant option since main-plan epics may not depend on branch epics |\n150\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008, E001 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 3 | Topology outcome selects which branch exists (`remove` if the other outcome holds) |\n151\t| E002 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 6 | Productization code lands in the midstream repo |\n152\t| E003 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 9 | Productized images carry license-cleared dependencies |\n153\t| BRANCH-A-E008 → BRANCH-A-E009, BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 13 | Platform Operator enablement builds against the CRs/manifests the productization epic produces |\n154\t| (no edge) E004 ↔ BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding and general implementation run in parallel; coupling enforced by \"build pipeline green\" AC |\n155\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002, E001 ∥ E003 | Rules 14/17 | Topology investigation, repo fork, and license scan have independent inputs; the repo and license work is topology-independent |\n156\t| (no edge) E005 ∥ E006 ∥ E004 | Rules 14/15 | Different repos/areas, no shared artifacts |\n157\t\n158\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n159\t\n160\t| HLR | Priority | Covered by |\n161\t|---|---|---|\n162\t| HLR-1 — supported Feature Store enablement via Platform Operator with productized images | P0 | E002, E003, E004 (onboarding + productized image chain); BRANCH-A-E008 + BRANCH-A-E009 or BRANCH-B-E008 + BRANCH-B-E009 (topology-specific deployment and enablement, exactly one branch executes) |\n163\t| HLR-2 — Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | P1 | E005 |\n164\t| HLR-3 — Dashboard shows Feature Store, links to endpoints per project | P1 | E006 |\n165\t| HLR-4 — product documentation (enablement, getting started, limits) | P2 | E007 |\n166\t\n167\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E001–E004 inherit P0\n168\tfrom HLR-1 (E001 blocks all P0 work → implicitly P0). E007 is a `docs-authoring` epic:\n169\tpriority-exception applies — strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (not\n170\tinherited from the implementations it depends on).\n171\t\n172\t## Health Warnings\n173\t\n174\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): no Impacted Teams table, no\n175\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no NFRs. Team\n176\t  assignments were inferred (Dashboard from its architecture-context file; others\n177\t  named after their components) and per-epic ACs were derived from the HLRs. Human\n178\t  verification of team assignments recommended.\n179\t- **Missing architecture context for Platform Operator and Notebooks**: neither has a\n180\t  file under `.context/architecture-context/`. The strategy's own text establishes\n181\t  both as existing platform facilities (\"through the Platform Operator like any other\n182\t  managed component\"; \"at least one supported workbench image\"), so they were NOT\n183\t  given new-compone