{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86b38a5e4adf55ab","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Select the Feast deployment topology for productization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Select the Feast deployment topology for productization\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve which Feast deployment topology RHOAI productizes first — the operator-based\n30\tdeployment or the standalone server per project — and produce a decision record that\n31\tall downstream Feature Store, Platform Operator, and Dashboard work builds on. Upstream\n32\tFeast supports both; supportability differs, and the choice determines what gets\n33\tpackaged, how administrators enable the component, and where per-project endpoints\n34\tcome from.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Evaluate the operator-based deployment topology: deployment complexity, upgrade\n39\t  path, multi-project behavior, resource footprint, security posture, support surface.\n40\t- Evaluate the standalone-server-per-project topology against the same criteria.\n41\t- Validate both topologies in a test environment (a live OpenShift cluster).\n42\t- Document the decision: selected topology, rationale, rejected alternative, and\n43\t  consequences for Platform Operator enablement, per-project endpoint exposure, and\n44\t  Dashboard integration.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Both topologies